      "claim": "An \"executive order\" is a directive that, by definition and statutory interpretation, can be issued only by the President of the United States.",
      "evidence": "3 U.S.C. § 19 defines executive orders as \"orders issued by the President\"; legal scholarship (e.g., the Congressional Research Service report on executive orders) and Supreme Court precedent (Youngstown Sheet & Tube Co. v. Sawyer, 1952) treat executive orders as uniquely presidential instruments.",
      "weight": 0.30,
      "depends_on": []
